{"_id":"6ad7d179a4131568064faebb","id":"alexar76/histor-mcp-tool-definitions","author":"alexar76","sha":"aaa97e832e94533dd9a80909ddb8762f273707c2","lastModified":"2026-10-26T13:52:53.000Z","private":false,"gated":false,"disabled":false,"tags":["language:en","license:cc-by-4.0","size_categories:100K<n<1M","format:json","modality:tabular","modality:text","library:datasets","library:pandas","library:polars","library:mlcroissant","region:us","mcp","model-context-protocol","ai-security","prompt-injection","tool-poisoning","transparency-log"],"description":"\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tHISTOR snapshot 2026-10-26: what MCP servers advertise, and when it changes\n\t\n\nHISTOR reads the tool list (tools/list) of every remote MCP server in the official MCP registry\non a polling schedule, and of npm/PyPI MCP packages run in a sandbox once per published version (new versions\nfirst, a few hundred a day). It records the exact tool definitions,\npins them by digest, and writes a signed label to a public RFC 9162 Merkle log whenever a tool set\nfirst appears, stays the same, or… See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/alexar76/histor-mcp-tool-definitions.","downloads":111,"likes":0,"cardData":{"license":"cc-by-4.0","pretty_name":"HISTOR — MCP tool definitions and how they change","language":["en"],"tags":["mcp","model-context-protocol","ai-security","prompt-injection","tool-poisoning","transparency-log"],"size_categories":["10K<n<100K"],"configs":[{"config_name":"servers","data_files":"servers.jsonl.gz"},{"config_name":"toolsets","data_files":"toolsets.jsonl.gz"},{"config_name":"changes","data_files":"changes.jsonl.gz"},{"config_name":"scans","data_files":"scans.jsonl.gz"},{"config_name":"classifications","data_files":"classifications.jsonl.gz"},{"config_name":"tool_extras","data_files":"tool_extras.jsonl.gz"},{"config_name":"extras_changes","data_files":"extras_changes.jsonl.gz"},{"config_name":"package_observations","data_files":"package_observa